  -
    id task.json-transform
    type task
    name Transform JSON
    summary Parse a JSON document, update a nested value, and emit JSON again.
    level 0
    tags
      - task
      - json
    card `parse -> mutate -> stringify`
    intent
      - edit json
      - transform json
      - 修改JSON
    relations
      requires
        - syntax.json
        - idiom.json-roundtrip
    examples
      -
        code `var doc = '{"items": [{"n": 1}, {"n": 2}]}'.getJson(json: true);
for i = 0 to doc.items.@count() - 1 do
  doc.items[i].n *= 10;
end do;
?. doc.@toJson(json: true);
`
        expect `{"items":[{"n":10},{"n":20}]}
`

  -
    id task.hello-server
    type task
    name A tiny HTTP JSON endpoint
    summary Create `HttpServer(port)`, register a handler that writes JSON, and call `run()`. Requires a listening socket; not executed by the ontology checker.
    level 1
    tags
      - task
      - http
    card `HttpServer(8080).get('/health', handler)`
    intent
      - web server
      - health endpoint
      - 接口服务
    relations
      requires
        - module.http-server
    examples
      -
        code `use 'http-server.fun';
fun health(req, res)
  res.json([ok: true]);
end fun;
var s = HttpServer(8080);
s.get('/health', health);
s.run();
`
        runnable false

